==English==
===Etymology===
{{onomatopoeia}}. Connected with {{term|splash}} and {{term|splish}} by vowel {{w|apophony}} (sound change); compare with {{w|Indo-European ablaut}} as in {{term|sing|lang=en}}/{{term|sang|lang=en}}/{{term|sung|lang=en}}/{{term|song|lang=en}}. Compare also {{term|slosh|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
*: {{rhymes|ɒʃ}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|splosh|es}}

# to make the sound of [[splash|splashing]]
# to [[traverse]] [[mushy]], [[marshy]] or otherwise [[viscus]] land
# to [[spill]] or [[spill over]]

====Related terms====
* [[splash]]
* [[splish]]

